## Operator patterns (repeat these — do not revert)

These are fixes the operator applies via Grafana Assistant / UI. **Do not overwrite with hand-rolled alternatives.**

| Topic | Use (operator pattern) | Do not use |
|-------|------------------------|------------|
| **Memory %** | `kentik_snmp_MemoryUtilization{$sel}` | `100 * MemoryUsed / (MemoryUsed + MemoryAvailable)`; `last_over_time` ratio hacks |
| **Interface bps** | `(kentik_snmp_ifHCInOctets{...}) * 8 / 60` | `rate(kentik_snmp_ifHC*Octets[...])` |
| **Interface errors/s** | `(kentik_snmp_ifInErrors{...}) / 60` | `rate(kentik_snmp_if*Errors[...])` |
| **Flow bytes** | `max_over_time(network_io_by_flow_bytes[...])` | `rate(network_io_by_flow_bytes[...])` |
| **Trap volume** | Loki: `count_over_time({service_name=~"ktranslate.*"} \|~ "(?i)(KSnmpTrap\|linkDown\|…)" [$__interval])` | `rate(kentik_ktranslate_chf_kkc_snmp_traps[5m])` |
| **Syslog volume** | Loki: `sum by (severity) (count_over_time({service_name=~"ktranslate.*"} \| json \| severity != "" [$__interval]))` | `rate(kentik_ktranslate_chf_kkc_syslog_messages[5m])` |
| **CHF metrics** | Collector health / heartbeat panels only | Event volume or device telemetry |
| **Fleet count stats** | `count(...) OR vector(0)` | Bare `count(...)` → "No data" |
| **Δ24h stats** | `instant: false` on stat; current expr minus `offset 24h` subquery | Single instant snapshot |
| **Timeseries trends** | `instant: false`, range query | `instant: true` on timeseries |
| **BGP state** | `tBgpPeerNgConnState="established"` / `!="established"` | Magic `== 6` (acceptable in legacy panels; prefer strings in new work) |
| **SNMP tables** | `labelsToFields` → `merge` → `organize`; hide `deployment_host`, `src_addr`, … | Raw instant tables; missing `merge` (shows 1 row only) |
| **Device drill-down** | `/d/ktranslate-device-details?var-instance=${__data.fields.device_name}` | Legacy `magz6qw1` UID |
| **New Device Details UI** | Follow `local/docs/grafana-network-dashboard-design-patterns.md` | Ad-hoc layout/naming/table transforms |

**SNMP inventory:** `count by (device_name) (kentik_snmp_CPU)` — **not** `kentik_snmp_DeviceMetrics` (AWS path only).

